{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>וַתַּמְרוּ וגו׳ וַתָּזִידוּ.</b> Meaning: they rebelled against the word of HaShem, who had told them not to ascend. Moreover, there was an additional reason why they should have been all the more careful not to defy Him, for it was He who brought their enemies against them — and this would demonstrate the willfulness of their hearts; this is what the verse means by <b>וַתָּזִידוּ</b> and so on. Further, it may intend that they did not make the ascent up the mountain out of great trust in HaShem so as to repair the deficiency in the trust and faith they had in Him — for they had said that He could not, perish the thought, save them and dispossess the nations — but rather in willfulness you did the thing, without submission and humility and seeking repair before HaShem. Therefore, ״וַיֵּצֵא הָאֱמוֹרִי״ and so on."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:14:24.943646411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}